  "system_prompt": "You are a senior medicinal chemist specializing in prodrug design and ADMET optimization. Always respond with valid JSON containing a 'modifications' list. Each modification must include 'description', 'smiles', and 'rationale' fields.",
  "user_prompt": "As a medicinal chemist, optimize Oseltamivir (SMILES: CCOC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](N)C1) as a prodrug for enhanced bioavailability and target-specific activation against Influenza Neuraminidase. Suggest SMILES modifications that improve ADMET while maintaining or enhancing activity.\n\nRespond ONLY with JSON in this exact format:\n{\"modifications\": [{\"description\": \"modification description\", \"smiles\": \"MODIFIED_SMILES_STRING\", \"rationale\": \"scientific rationale\"}]}",
  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a phosphate ester to enhance water solubility and facilitate activation by phosphatases in vivo.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCOP(=O)(OCC(O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](N)C1)O\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Phosphate prodrugs are commonly used to improve the solubility of hydrophobic drugs and are efficiently cleaved by ubiquitous phosphatases in the body, enabling the release of the active drug.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add a valine ester moiety to improve intestinal permeability through peptide transporters.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCOC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](N)C1COC(=O)C(C)NC(C)C\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Valine esters can enhance bioavailability by exploiting peptide transporter 1 (PEPT1) in the gastrointestinal tract, increasing drug absorption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Incorporate a carbamate linkage to mask the amine group and improve stability during gastrointestinal transit.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"CCOC(=O)C1=C[C@@H](OC(CC)CC)[C@@H](NC(C)=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)OCH3)C1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Carbamate prodrugs enhance chemical stability by reducing the reactivity of the free amine group, while being cleaved by enzymes like esterases to release the active drug.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
